              "text": "In Telangana, the division of legislative and parliamentary representation is structured as follows:\n\n### 1. MLA (Member of Legislative Assembly) Seats\n* **Total MLA Seats:** **119**\n* These are the directly elected representatives representing the 119 assembly constituencies of the state in the Telangana Legislative Assembly (Lower House of the State Legislature).\n\n### 2. MP (Member of Parliament) Seats\nMembers of Parliament represent Telangana in both the lower and upper houses of India's Parliament:\n* **Lok Sabha (Lower House) MP Seats:** **17**\n* **Rajya Sabha (Upper House) MP Seats:** **7**\n* **Total MP Seats:** **24** (17 Lok Sabha + 7 Rajya Sabha)\n\n---\n\n### Additional Context:\n* **MLC (Member of Legislative Council) Seats:** **40**. Telangana has a bicameral legislature, meaning it also has an upper house called the Legislative Council (Vidhan Parishad), which consists of 40 members.\n* **Upcoming Changes (Delimitation):** Under proposed national delimitation plans, the central government has introduced bills to redraw constituency boundaries. Once implemented, Telangana's seats are projected to increase to approximately **26 Lok Sabha (MP) seats** and **179 to 182 Assembly (MLA) seats**. However, the current active strength remains 17 MP seats and 119 MLA seats.",
